      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That's about twice the labeled maximum daily dose:\n\n- Immediate-release: 2,550 mg/day (usually 850 mg three times daily with meals)\n- Extended-release: 2,000 to 2,500 mg/day, depending on the product\n\nDoses this high raise the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity. Normal kidney and liver function doesn't change the labeled limit.\n\nThe dose may be a typo. Possible intended orders include:\n- 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day)\n- 500 mg PO three times daily with meals (1,500 mg/day)\n- 1,700 mg total per day, for example 850 mg PO twice daily\n\nTell me the dose you want, and I'll enter it right away. If you do intend a dose above the labeled maximum, it needs to go through pharmacy or the prescriber of record. I can't enter it on a verbal confirmation."
      }
